{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/47115-what-is-geist-baby-don-t-hurt-me","id":47115,"title":"What is Geist (baby, don't hurt me...)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-11T15:58:33-08:00","id":47115,"title":"What is Geist (baby, don't hurt me...)","content":"Okay, as silly as the title sounds, what exactly is the backstory behind Geists? I know they are people that have risen from the dead, with unknown ghost-like entities attached to their souls (or something along those lines), but what are their main motivations and fears? I know that Vampires have their Damnation and the Danse Macabre, I know that Werewolves are spirit-police hunted by the Pure, and I know about Mages being in a fallen world controlled by the Exarchs, but what is the story behind Geist? What are their main motivations and fears and enemies?<br /> <br /> Also, what powers and/or weaknesses do they generally possess? Yes, I'm sure they are quite diverse and not easy to describe in one sentence, but a few guidelines, just to know if it's something that I'd be interested in, something worth picking up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:27:13-08:00","id":47141,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here's the thing: Sin-Eater culture's big monolithic political entities have either gone way underground or outright collapsed into whatever remnants their older members could carry away. Imagine Werewolf without the Father Wolf mythos, or Mage without the Atlantis story. That's the state Bound culture is in right now; there is no most-popular-monomyth, and every krewe has a different explanation for why ghosts turned into the land of the dead's equivalent of spirits have given them a second chance at life in exchange for maybe-not-entirely-pretending to be their past-life personas.<br /> <br /> The big theme of the game is, essentially, &quot;Now what?&quot; (It is worth noting here the original and literal definition of &quot;apocalypse,&quot; as those are essentially what the Bound's proto-Y/Z-splat take as their guiding stars.)<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, their powers evoke ghostly or deathly phenomena \u2014 there's an entire Manifestation called the Curse, for instance \u2014 and the general phenomena associated with mediums; there are two different classes of extrasensory Manifestation. Broadly, there's five Thresholds (types of death, loosely arranged between the five Horsemen of the apocalypse) and ten/seven Keys (&quot;half&quot; of which use the Occult Skill [the four Elemental Keys have significant overlap]; each Threshold gives its Sin-Eaters one of two Keys, and each of those pairs includes an Occult Key) Sin-Eaters most commonly deal with. There's also ceremonies that leverage the power of the Underworld through ritual invocation of the geist's connection to the Great Below.<br /> <br /> Antagonists generally include those who mess with the boundary between life and death. Comparisons to Werewolf arise here, and, as there, &quot;ghost cop&quot; would be a gross mis-simplification of the &quot;duty&quot; \u2014 which the Bound, naturally, don't universally agree is a duty; &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is the cultural term for those that do see it as one \u2014 the Forsaken and the Bound both approach their respective ephemeral worlds with an eye toward figuring out and enacting their particular policies upon the Earthly affairs of those ephemeral beings; just as some werewolves might allow fire-spirits to inhabit the local crematorium as long as they don't start any shit on their turf, a krewe of Sin-Eaters might take a hardline stance against letting ghosts deliver their last regrets in person but have no problem conveying messages from beyond the grave \u2014 the biggest difference is that the werewolves are more territorial.<br /> <br /> Weaknesses tend to arise electively from krewe culture once it's grown to at least the scope of a citywide organization, in much the same way that packs trade adherence to a ban for boons from their totem. Every &quot;official&quot; krewe has a basic ban, duty, and ethos that any member can opt into to better stabilize their bond with their geist, and stronger ones can gain some affinity for a particular Key in exchange for some manner of weakness, whether it's a baneful substance, an atrophied Attribute, or an incurable derangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:18:23-08:00","id":47279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/47115-what-is-geist-baby-don-t-hurt-me?p=47141#post47141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weaknesses tend to arise electively from krewe culture once it's grown to at least the scope of a citywide organization, in much the same way that packs trade adherence to a ban for boons from their totem. Every &quot;official&quot; krewe has a basic ban, duty, and ethos that any member can opt into to better stabilize their bond with their geist, and stronger ones can gain some affinity for a particular Key in exchange for some manner of weakness, whether it's a baneful substance, an atrophied Attribute, or an incurable derangement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, though the Ethos is comprised of Ban, Duty, and Destiny, which acts as the true force that reveals the secret of the Underworld, given spiritual mystique through the Mythos of the Krewe. Remember that despite it's operation, every krewe becomes a death religion is one way or another, even if the members may not realize it. That is the purpose of a bonded krewe, to discover a facet and uncover powers of the Underworld that is more or less brought into being by they and their Geist's belief and desire. Humorously, in my opinion Sin-Eaters resemble Orks due to their powers and understanding of the Underworld being influenced heavily by their belief of how death works, and thanks to a bonded Krewe's channel, every single krewe's beliefs about the Great Below are true to a large extent-making them the &quot;orkiest&quot; splat besides Mages or Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}